#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""PLAN.md 2.30: the end-to-end test, against the Compose stack's own images.

It brings up postgres, bucket, ace, the parser, sandbox and network pools and the e2e profile's
responder under a project of its own (ace4-e2e), with:

- a signatures repository it makes under target/e2e/ from tools/ace3/trees/signatures, holding
  one rule that matches a marker string only in a file tagged type=email.attachment (its meta_tags
  directive);
- tests/e2e/site/overlay.yaml, which points the RDAP module and the proxy_domain_splunk instance
  of the Splunk module at the responder's recordings, so nothing reaches the internet;
- a 15-second lease, so a task a killed pool held comes back quickly.

It makes an API key holding alert:create with `ace user create-key` in the ace container, since the
stack has no default key (PLAN.md 5.5), and submits through the JSON API with it, as `ace compare`
does below. It checks the GUI's login page and its Datastar on the same port (PLAN.md 5.7). Then it
submits samples/ace4/email/e2e.email.rfc822, an email with a DKIM signing domain
(example.com) in its headers and a zip attachment holding the marker, twice. Each time, the email, archive and YARA modules run in
email mode; the YARA match on the attachment makes the root an alert in correlation mode, which
runs RDAP and the Splunk instance, the delayed module, on the domain. The email goes in with the
original_email directive, as ace3's collectors give it, so the email logger runs once the rest of the
root is done and records the email's thread in brocess with its task's end, which the thread module,
running for correlation, waits for and then reads back (PLAN.md 7.4). The second time the
parser pool is frozen before the submission, so the core leases it a task it never answers, and
it is killed with SIGKILL while it holds that lease, then started again. Both roots must have
results from all five modules and complete; the second only later. The same email goes in both
times, so their trees in the normal form (PLAN.md 3.1) must be the same text, which goes to
<work>/normal-form.json.

Then the browser test (PLAN.md 5.8, 5.9 and 5.10): the e2e profile's headless Chromium, pinned by digest in
compose.yaml, logs in to the GUI as an analyst that `ace user create-first` makes and opens a third
submission's alert page while the network pool is frozen, so the page has no RDAP result. The pool is
let go, and the RDAP result has to appear on the open page, pushed by its live stream, with no reload
and nothing the page's Content-Security-Policy refused. Then it opens the alert list (5.10) filtered to
open alerts, which shows that alert, and a filter that matches nothing, which lists nothing; it opens
the open alerts again, dispositions the alert through the JSON API with a key of its own, and the
list's refresh has to drop it from the open page, again with no reload and nothing refused. It drives
the browser over the DevTools protocol, with a WebSocket client here, so it needs nothing more than
python3. Before the list, it opens that alert's relationship graph (5.13) from the alert page's link and
checks that vis.js drew a node for the alert and each of its observables, results and tags, with nothing
refused and nothing thrown.

It also runs a GUI command (PLAN.md 5.12): signed in as that analyst, it starts `ace --help` and `ace serve`
through the JSON API with the session, which the parser pool runs contained, and checks that the help
completed with ace's usage and that `serve` was refused, as a command a contained process can't run.

Then the analyst-edited lists (PLAN.md 5.14): signed in as that analyst, it adds the email's sender to the
sender whitelist through the JSON API and submits the email once more, with nothing restarted. The email
module has to whitelist it, the root's analysis has to stop with nothing extracted and no alert, and the
entry's audit row has to name the analyst. It deletes the entry the same way before anything else runs,
so the comparison below sees the empty whitelists ace3's trees were made with. Before the comparison it
gives ace4 what make-trees gave ace3's tagging and detection modules (PLAN.md 7.6): the observables
enabled for detection in tools/ace3/trees/detections.json, added through the detection API with a key
holding detection:write, and the tags of tools/ace3/trees/observable_tags.json, with SQL; the site
tagger's rows are in the overlay.

Then the scanners (PLAN.md 7.7): it builds ace4-js-deobfuscator and ace4-phishkit from ace3's checkout
with docker/scanners/build when this host hasn't them, and the stack's scanner pool runs them, phishkit's
on the e2e profile's internal network, `scanned`. It submits samples/ace4/web/phishkit_page.html as an
email's attachment named phishkit_page.htm, the one extension tests/e2e/site/overlay.yaml lets phishkit render, in correlation mode, and phishkit_analyzer has to render it and javascript_deobfuscation
run the script html_js_extraction writes out of it, each through a scan the queue held while its task
waited. Then it submits the page again and dispositions the root while its phishkit scan runs, and the
pool has to kill the scanner and remove its container; and again, and kills the pool with SIGKILL while
the scanner runs, and the pool has to remove the container it left when it starts again, while the core
ends the scan abandoned once its lease runs out and the module says so. ace3's scanner managers, and any
container they started, have to be as they were.

Then the library diff's self-test runs (PLAN.md 4.8), and tools/ace3/modules/check checks the module
inventory, docs/modules.md, against ace3's config at the head of ace3's checkout (PLAN.md 7.1), and its
modules that read ACE's own data against ace3's code, each with what serves it (7.2), and its modules
that start a process, each with a decision for every program (7.3); under CI, which has no ace3
checkout, that check is skipped.

It then runs `ace compare` (PLAN.md 3.3, crates/ace-app/src/compare.rs) over the sample set, each
sample in the cli mode against ace3's tree in tools/ace3/trees/reference/ (3.2), and writes the
report to <work>/compare/. It enforces the acceptance threshold in docs/acceptance.md: a difference
in any sample that tools/ace3/trees/differences.md doesn't list fails the test, and so does a row
that matches nothing, so the list stays true. So does a sample absent from this machine, unless CI
is set: CI doesn't have the git-ignored samples/local/, so there it holds over the tracked samples,
and the report says how many were absent.

Usage: tests/e2e/run [--keep] [--compare]
  --keep      leaves the stack up
  --compare   only brings up the stack and runs `ace compare` over the sample set, reporting
              differences without enforcing the threshold, and fails only when a sample can't be
              run

Exits 0 when every check passes. Needs docker compose and python3 on the host.

A site repository runs the same scenario, without the comparison with ace3, against its own images (PLAN.md 2.32) by setting:

- ACE4_E2E_COMPOSE: its Compose file, whose services have this file's names (postgres, bucket,
  ace, parsers, lookups and the e2e profile's responder);
- ACE4_E2E_PREFIX: the prefix of that file's variables, such as SITE_PORT_, in place of ACE4_;
- ACE4_E2E_PROJECT: the Compose project the test runs under, in place of ace4-e2e;
- ACE4_E2E_SITE: the site overlay directory, in place of tests/e2e/site;
- ACE4_E2E_WORK: where the signatures repository goes, in place of target/e2e;
- ACE4_E2E_PORT: the host port, as for ace4;
- ACE4_E2E_ACE_COMMAND: the ace service's binary, in place of ace.

Its modules differ from ace3's by design, so setting ACE4_E2E_SITE skips the comparison.
"""

import base64
import hashlib
import http.client
import json
import os
import re
import shutil
import socket
import struct
import subprocess
import sys
import time
import urllib.parse
import urllib.request
import uuid
from pathlib import Path

ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent.parent
COMPOSE_FILE = Path(os.environ.get("ACE4_E2E_COMPOSE", ROOT / "compose.yaml")).resolve()
PREFIX = os.environ.get("ACE4_E2E_PREFIX", "ACE4_")
WORK = Path(os.environ.get("ACE4_E2E_WORK", ROOT / "target" / "e2e")).resolve()
SITE = Path(os.environ.get("ACE4_E2E_SITE", ROOT / "tests" / "e2e" / "site")).resolve()
PROJECT = os.environ.get("ACE4_E2E_PROJECT", "ace4-e2e")
PORT = os.environ.get("ACE4_E2E_PORT", "7444")
ACE_COMMAND = os.environ.get("ACE4_E2E_ACE_COMMAND", "ace")
LEASE_SECONDS = 15
RULE = "ace4_e2e_attachment"
SAMPLE = "ace4/email/e2e.email.rfc822"
EMAIL_SAMPLE = ROOT / "samples" / SAMPLE
TREES = ROOT / "tools" / "ace3" / "trees"
MODULES = [
    "email_analyzer",
    "archive",
    "yara_scanner_v3_4",
    "rdap_analyzer",
    "proxy_domain_splunk",
]

ENV = {
    **os.environ,
    **{
        PREFIX + name: value
        for name, value in {
            "STACK": PROJECT,
            "PORT_HTTPS": PORT,
            "SITE": str(SITE),
            "SIGNATURES": str(WORK / "signatures"),
            "LEASE_SECONDS": str(LEASE_SECONDS),
            "RULESET_POLL_SECONDS": "2",
            "POOL_RULESET_POLL_SECONDS": "2",
            # the recorded Splunk takes any password
            "SPLUNK_PASSWORD": "ace4-fake-password",
            # phishkit's containers go on the e2e profile's internal network, which reaches the
            # responder and nothing outside the stack (compose.yaml's `scanned`)
            "PHISHKIT_NETWORK": f"{PROJECT}_scanned",
        }.items()
    },
}
ENV.pop("COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME", None)
COMPOSE = ["docker", "compose", "-f", str(COMPOSE_FILE), "--profile", "e2e"]
SERVICES = ["postgres", "bucket", "ace", "parsers", "sandbox", "lookups", "scanners", "responder"]
# PLAN.md 7.7: the page the scanner checks render, and its inline script the deobfuscator runs
SCANNER_PAGE = ROOT / "samples" / "ace4" / "web" / "phishkit_page.html"
SCANNER_IMAGES = ["ace4-js-deobfuscator:latest", "ace4-phishkit:latest"]
# The analyst the browser test logs in as, and the GUI as the browser reaches it on the stack's network.
ANALYST = "e2e-analyst"
ANALYST_PASSWORD = "e2e analyst password, not a secret"
GUI_IN_STACK = "http://ace:8000"
# Ports of Python libraries: each must have results from both systems, because a comparison with
# nothing compared passes.
LIBRARY_PORTS = [
    "msoffice_encryption_analyzer", "olevba_v1_2", "pcodedmp", "pdf_analyzer", "rtfole",
    "xlmdeobfuscator",
]


def log(message):
    print(f"e2e: {message}", flush=True)


def compose(*args, check=True, capture=False, exit_code=False):
    result = subprocess.run(
        [*COMPOSE, *args], env=ENV, cwd=COMPOSE_FILE.parent, text=True, capture_output=capture
    )
    if exit_code:
        return result.returncode
    if check and result.returncode != 0:
        raise SystemExit(
            f"e2e: docker compose {' '.join(args)} failed ({result.returncode})\n"
            f"{result.stderr if capture else ''}"
        )
    return result.stdout if capture else ""


def sql(query):
    """Rows of a query against the stack's Postgres, as lists of strings."""
    # the database and user the stack's Compose file gave the postgres service
    out = compose(
        "exec", "-T", "-e", f"QUERY={query}", "postgres", "sh", "-c",
        'psql -U "$POSTGRES_USER" -d "$POSTGRES_DB" -At -F "\t" -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 -c "$QUERY"',
        capture=True,
    )
    return [line.split("\t") for line in out.splitlines() if line]


def git(*args):
    subprocess.run(
        ["git", "-C", str(WORK / "signatures"), "-c", "user.name=ace4 e2e",
         "-c", "user.email=e2e@example.invalid", "-c", "commit.gpgsign=false",
         "-c", "init.defaultBranch=main", *args],
        check=True, capture_output=True,
    )


def make_signatures():
    """A repository with tools/ace3/trees/signatures' one fixture rule, the rule ace3's trees
    scanned with, committed. Returns its commit."""
    repo = WORK / "signatures"
    shutil.rmtree(repo, ignore_errors=True)
    shutil.copytree(ROOT / "tools" / "ace3" / "trees" / "signatures", repo / "yara")
    git("init", "-q")
    git("add", ".")
    git("commit", "-q", "-m", "the end-to-end test's rule")
    return subprocess.run(
        ["git", "-C", str(repo), "rev-parse", "HEAD"], check=True, capture_output=True,
        text=True,
    ).stdout.strip()


def make_key():
    """An API key that can submit, made in the ace container, which holds the database. The key goes
    to `ace compare` through ACE4_API_KEY in this process's environment, not its command line."""
    out = compose(
        "exec", "-T", "ace", ACE_COMMAND, "user", "create-key", "e2e-submitter",
        "--grant", "alert:create", capture=True,
    )
    token = next(
        (line.split(": ", 1)[1] for line in out.splitlines()
         if line.startswith("token (shown once): ")),
        None,
    )
    if not token:
        raise SystemExit(f"e2e: `ace user create-key` printed no token:\n{out}")
    ENV["ACE4_API_KEY"] = token
    return token


def submit(email, mode="email", observables=()):
    """Submits a root, with the email as its file if there is one, and returns its uuid."""
    boundary = f"ace4-e2e-{uuid.uuid4().hex}"
    analysis = json.dumps({
        "description": "ace4 end-to-end test",
        "analysis_mode": mode,
        "observables": list(observables),
    })
    body = (
        f"--{boundary}\r\nContent-Disposition: form-data; name=\"analysis\"\r\n\r\n"
        f"{analysis}\r\n"
    ).encode()
    if email is not None:
        body += (
            f"--{boundary}\r\nContent-Disposition: form-data; name=\"file\"; "
            f"filename=\"email.rfc822\"\r\nContent-Type: message/rfc822\r\n\r\n"
        ).encode() + email + b"\r\n"
    body += f"--{boundary}--\r\n".encode()
    request = urllib.request.Request(
        f"http://127.0.0.1:{PORT}/api/analysis/v1/submit",
        data=body,
        method="POST",
        headers={
            "Authorization": f"Bearer {ENV['ACE4_API_KEY']}",
            "Content-Type": f"multipart/form-data; boundary={boundary}",
        },
    )
    with urllib.request.urlopen(request, timeout=30) as response:
        if response.status != 201:
            raise SystemExit(f"e2e: the submission answered {response.status}")
        return json.load(response)["id"]


def submit_file(data, name, mode, yara_meta=()):
    """Submits a root with one file at `name`, with these yara_meta tags, and returns its uuid."""
    boundary = f"ace4-e2e-{uuid.uuid4().hex}"
    analysis = json.dumps({
        "description": "ace4 end-to-end test",
        "analysis_mode": mode,
        "file_yara_meta": {name: list(yara_meta)},
    })
    body = (
        f"--{boundary}\r\nContent-Disposition: form-data; name=\"analysis\"\r\n\r\n{analysis}\r\n"
        f"--{boundary}\r\nContent-Disposition: form-data; name=\"file\"; filename=\"{name}\"\r\n"
        f"Content-Type: application/octet-stream\r\n\r\n"
    ).encode() + data + f"\r\n--{boundary}--\r\n".encode()
    request = urllib.request.Request(
        f"http://127.0.0.1:{PORT}/api/analysis/v1/submit", data=body, method="POST",
        headers={"Authorization": f"Bearer {ENV['ACE4_API_KEY']}",
                 "Content-Type": f"multipart/form-data; boundary={boundary}"},
    )
    with urllib.request.urlopen(request, timeout=30) as response:
        if response.status != 201:
            raise SystemExit(f"e2e: the submission answered {response.status}")
        return json.load(response)["id"]


def build_scanner_images():
    """The scanner images (PLAN.md 7.7), built from ace3's checkout by docker/scanners/build when this
    host hasn't them. Without a checkout, as under CI, the test can't build them, and says so."""
    missing = [image for image in SCANNER_IMAGES if subprocess.run(
        ["docker", "image", "inspect", image], capture_output=True).returncode != 0]
    if not missing:
        return
    log(f"building the scanner images {missing} from ace3's sources")
    names = [image.removeprefix("ace4-").removesuffix(":latest") for image in missing]
    if subprocess.run([str(ROOT / "docker" / "scanners" / "build"), *names]).returncode != 0:
        raise SystemExit("e2e: docker/scanners/build failed; the scanner pool needs its images")


def scanner_containers(*labels):
    """The ids of the containers on this host's daemon with every one of `labels`, running or not."""
    out = subprocess.run(
        ["docker", "ps", "-a", "-q", *[a for label in labels for a in ("--filter", f"label={label}")]],
        capture_output=True, text=True, check=True,
    ).stdout
    return [line for line in out.split() if line]


def ace3_scanner_state():
    """ace3's scanner managers and the scanners they run, which nothing here may touch."""
    out = subprocess.run(
        ["docker", "ps", "-a", "--format", "{{.ID}} {{.Names}} {{.State}}",
         "--filter", "label=com.docker.compose.project=ace"],
        capture_output=True, text=True, check=True,
    ).stdout
    managers = sorted(line for line in out.splitlines() if "phishkit" in line or "deobfuscator" in line)
    return managers, scanner_containers("phishkit.job_id")


def running_scan(root, within=120):
    """The id of the root's phishkit scan once its pool has started its container, and the container."""
    def found():
        rows = sql(f"""SELECT id FROM queue.scans WHERE root_id = '{root}' AND scanner = 'phishkit'
                       AND state = 'running'""")
        if not rows:
            return None
        containers = scanner_containers(f"ace4.scanner.stack={PROJECT}", f"ace4.scanner.scan={rows[0][0]}")
        return (rows[0][0], containers[0]) if containers else None
    return wait_for(f"root {root}'s phishkit scan to start its container", found, within=within)


def check_scanners(failures):
    """PLAN.md 7.7's Done check: phishkit_analyzer and javascript_deobfuscation results come through
    the queue, from scans the scanner pool ran in ace3's scanner images; a cancelled root's scanner is
    killed and its container removed; a scanner a crashed pool left is removed when the pool starts
    again, and its scan ends abandoned; and nothing of ace3's is touched."""

    def expect(ok, message):
        log(("ok    " if ok else "FAIL  ") + message)
        if not ok:
            failures.append(message)

    ace3_before = ace3_scanner_state()
    page = SCANNER_PAGE.read_bytes()
    # an email's HTML attachment in correlation mode, which phishkit renders, and whose inline script
    # html_js_extraction writes out for the deobfuscator
    root = submit_file(page, "phishkit_page.htm", "correlation", ["type=email.attachment"])
    wait_for(f"root {root} to finish", lambda: completed_after(root) is not None, within=240)
    phishkit = sql(
        f"""SELECT r.details->>'scan_type', r.details->>'exit_code', coalesce(r.details->>'error', ''),
                   jsonb_array_length(r.details->'output_files'), r.summary
            FROM analysis.results r WHERE r.root_id = '{root}' AND r.module = 'phishkit_analyzer'"""
    )
    expect(len(phishkit) == 1 and phishkit[0][:3] == ["file", "0", ""] and int(phishkit[0][3]) >= 2,
           f"phishkit_analyzer rendered the page in its scanner: {phishkit}")
    files = sql(
        f"""SELECT f.path FROM analysis.files f WHERE f.root_id = '{root}' AND f.path LIKE 'phishkit/%'"""
    )
    expect(any(row[0].endswith("/screenshot.png") for row in files),
           f"its screenshot is a file in the alert: {[row[0] for row in files]}")
    deobfuscated = sql(
        f"""SELECT f.path, r.details->>'event_count', r.details->>'exit_code'
            FROM analysis.results r JOIN analysis.files f
              ON f.root_id = r.root_id AND f.observable_id = r.observable_id
            WHERE r.root_id = '{root}' AND r.module = 'javascript_deobfuscation'"""
    )
    expect(any(row[2] == "0" and row[1] not in ("0", None) for row in deobfuscated),
           f"javascript_deobfuscation ran the page's script in its scanner: {deobfuscated}")
    trace = sql(
        f"""SELECT f.path FROM analysis.files f WHERE f.root_id = '{root}'
            AND f.path LIKE '%deobfuscated-%'"""
    )
    expect(bool(trace), f"the deobfuscator's trace is a file in the alert: {trace}")
    scans = sql(f"SELECT scanner, state::text FROM queue.scans WHERE root_id = '{root}' ORDER BY id")
    expect(sorted(scans) == [["js-deobfuscator", "completed"], ["phishkit", "completed"]],
           f"the root's two scans ran through the queue and completed: {scans}")
    left = scanner_containers(f"ace4.scanner.stack={PROJECT}")
    expect(not left, f"no scanner container is left: {left}")

    # cancelled while its scanner runs: the pool kills it at its next renewal and removes it
    root = submit_file(page, "phishkit_page.htm", "correlation", ["type=email.attachment"])
    scan, container = running_scan(root)
    # dispositioning a root cancels its analysis (ace_service::Service::disposition)
    out = compose(
        "exec", "-T", "ace", ACE_COMMAND, "user", "create-key", "e2e-scan-canceller",
        "--grant", "alert:write", capture=True,
    )
    token = next((line.split(": ", 1)[1] for line in out.splitlines()
                  if line.startswith("token (shown once): ")), None)
    request = urllib.request.Request(
        f"http://127.0.0.1:{PORT}/api/alerts/v1/alerts/{root}/disposition",
        data=json.dumps({"disposition": "FALSE_POSITIVE"}).encode(), method="PUT",
        headers={"Authorization": f"Bearer {token}", "Content-Type": "application/json"},
    )
    with urllib.request.urlopen(request, timeout=30) as response:
        expect(response.status == 200, f"the scanned root was dispositioned: {response.status}")
    state = wait_for(f"scan {scan} to end", lambda: (sql(
        f"SELECT state::text FROM queue.scans WHERE id = {scan} AND state <> 'running'") or [[None]])[0][0],
        within=60)
    gone = wait_for(f"container {container} to go", lambda: not scanner_containers(
        f"ace4.scanner.scan={scan}", f"ace4.scanner.stack={PROJECT}") or None, within=30)
    expect(state == "cancelled" and gone, f"a cancelled root's scanner was killed and removed: {state}")

    # the pool dies with SIGKILL while its scanner runs: the scanner outlives it, and the pool removes
    # it when it starts again; the core ends the scan abandoned when its lease runs out
    root = submit_file(page, "phishkit_page.htm", "correlation", ["type=email.attachment"])
    scan, container = running_scan(root)
    compose("kill", "-s", "SIGKILL", "scanners")
    survived = bool(scanner_containers(f"ace4.scanner.scan={scan}", f"ace4.scanner.stack={PROJECT}"))
    compose("start", "scanners")
    gone = wait_for(f"the restarted pool to remove container {container}", lambda: not scanner_containers(
        f"ace4.scanner.scan={scan}", f"ace4.scanner.stack={PROJECT}") or None, within=60)
    expect(survived and gone, "a scanner the killed pool left was removed when the pool started again")
    wait_for(f"root {root} to finish", lambda: completed_after(root) is not None, within=240)
    abandoned = sql(f"SELECT state::text, error FROM queue.scans WHERE id = {scan}")
    error = sql(
        f"""SELECT r.details->>'error' FROM analysis.results r
            WHERE r.root_id = '{root}' AND r.module = 'phishkit_analyzer'"""
    )
    expect(abandoned and abandoned[0][0] == "abandoned"
           and bool(error) and "its pool stopped reporting on it" in (error[0][0] or ""),
           f"its scan ended abandoned, and the module says so: {abandoned} {error}")
    ace3_after = ace3_scanner_state()
    expect(ace3_after == ace3_before, f"ace3's scanner managers and scanners are as they were: {ace3_after}")


def check_gui(failures):
    """PLAN.md 5.7: `ace serve` serves the GUI on the JSON API's listener, with its security headers,
    and Datastar from the binary under a hashed name."""
    url = f"http://127.0.0.1:{PORT}"
    with urllib.request.urlopen(f"{url}/login", timeout=30) as response:
        page = response.read().decode()
        policy = response.headers.get("Content-Security-Policy", "")
    script = re.search(r'src="(/static/datastar-1\.0\.4\.[0-9a-f]{16}\.js)"', page)
    if "script-src 'self' 'nonce-" not in policy or script is None:
        log("FAIL  the GUI's login page isn't served with its policy and Datastar")
        failures.append("ace serve doesn't serve the GUI")
        return
    with urllib.request.urlopen(f"{url}{script.group(1)}", timeout=30) as response:
        digest = hashlib.sha256(response.read()).hexdigest()
    if digest != "727844adfc825ee651fb93c544a2a739986f9a21820a94524b35f0cac470cf91":
        log(f"FAIL  the GUI serves a Datastar with SHA-256 {digest}")
        failures.append("the GUI's Datastar isn't the vendored release")
        return
    log("ok    the GUI serves its login page and the vendored Datastar")


def wait_for(what, check, within, every=0.25):
    started = time.monotonic()
    while True:
        value = check()
        if value:
            return value
        if time.monotonic() - started > within:
            raise SystemExit(f"e2e: timed out after {within}s waiting for {what}")
        time.sleep(every)


def completed_after(root):
    """Seconds from the root's creation to its first completion, or None."""
    rows = sql(
        f"""SELECT extract(epoch FROM c.completed_at - r.created_at)
            FROM queue.root_completions c JOIN analysis.roots r ON r.id = c.root_id
            WHERE c.root_id = '{root}' ORDER BY c.pass LIMIT 1"""
    )
    return float(rows[0][0]) if rows else None


def tasks(root):
    return sql(
        f"""SELECT t.module, o.type, coalesce(f.path, o.value), t.state::text, t.attempts,
                   coalesce(t.error, '')
            FROM queue.tasks t JOIN analysis.observables o ON o.id = t.observable_id
            LEFT JOIN analysis.files f ON f.observable_id = o.id
            WHERE t.root_id = '{root}' ORDER BY t.id"""
    )


def check_root(root, failures):
    """Checks one root once it completed, adding a line to failures for each check that fails."""

    def expect(ok, message):
        log(("ok    " if ok else "FAIL  ") + message)
        if not ok:
            failures.append(f"{root}: {message}")

    modules = {row[0] for row in sql(
        f"SELECT DISTINCT module FROM analysis.results WHERE root_id = '{root}'"
    )}
    for module in MODULES:
        expect(module in modules, f"{module} has a result")
    mode, alerted, passes = sql(
        f"""SELECT analysis_mode, alerted_at IS NOT NULL, completed_pass = pass
            FROM analysis.roots WHERE id = '{root}'"""
    )[0]
    expect(mode == "correlation" and alerted == "t", "the YARA match made the root an alert")
    expect(passes == "t", "the root's pass completed")
    active = sql(
        f"""SELECT count(*) FROM queue.tasks WHERE root_id = '{root}'
            AND state IN ('queued', 'delayed', 'running')"""
    )[0][0]
    expect(active == "0", "no task is left queued, delayed or running")

    # the rule matched the attachment and not the extracted file, which holds the same marker;
    # a scan that matched nothing ends done with no result
    scans = {row[0]: (row[1], row[2] == "t") for row in sql(
        f"""SELECT f.path, t.state::text, coalesce(r.details::text LIKE '%{RULE}%', false)
            FROM queue.tasks t
            JOIN analysis.files f ON f.observable_id = t.observable_id AND f.root_id = t.root_id
            LEFT JOIN analysis.results r ON r.root_id = t.root_id
              AND r.observable_id = t.observable_id AND r.module = t.module
            WHERE t.root_id = '{root}' AND t.module = 'yara_scanner_v3_4'"""
    )}
    attachment = {p: v for p, v in scans.items() if p.endswith("invoice.zip")}
    extracted = {p: v for p, v in scans.items() if p.endswith("invoice.txt")}
    expect(bool(attachment) and all(v == ("done", True) for v in attachment.values()),
           f"the rule matched the tagged attachment: {attachment}")
    expect(bool(extracted) and all(v == ("done", False) for v in extracted.values()),
           f"the rule didn't match the untagged extracted file, which has the marker: "
           f"{extracted}")
    others = [p for p, v in scans.items() if v[1] and p not in attachment]
    expect(not others, f"the rule matched nothing else: {others}")

    rdap = sql(
        f"""SELECT o.value, r.details->>'lookup_protocol', coalesce(r.details->>'error', '')
            FROM analysis.results r JOIN analysis.observables o ON o.id = r.observable_id
            WHERE r.root_id = '{root}' AND r.module = 'rdap_analyzer'"""
    )
    expect(["example.com", "rdap", ""] in rdap,
           f"RDAP answered for example.com from the recording: {rdap}")
    splunk = sql(
        f"""SELECT o.value, coalesce(r.details->>'error', ''), t.attempts
            FROM analysis.results r JOIN analysis.observables o ON o.id = r.observable_id
            JOIN queue.tasks t ON t.root_id = r.root_id AND t.observable_id = r.observable_id
              AND t.module = r.module
            WHERE r.root_id = '{root}' AND r.module = 'proxy_domain_splunk'"""
    )
    expect(any(row[0] == "example.com" and row[1] == "" for row in splunk),
           f"the Splunk instance answered for example.com: {splunk}")
    delays = sql(
        f"""SELECT count(*) FROM queue.tasks
            WHERE root_id = '{root}' AND module = 'proxy_domain_splunk'
            AND first_delayed_at IS NOT NULL"""
    )[0][0]
    expect(delays != "0", "the Splunk task was delayed before its result")

    # PLAN.md 7.4: the email logger ran on the original email once the rest of the root was done,
    # stored no result, and its write landed with its task's end: the email is in brocess's thread
    # store, once however many roots it came in
    logger = sql(
        f"""SELECT t.state::text, (SELECT count(*) FROM analysis.results r
                                   WHERE r.root_id = t.root_id AND r.module = t.module)
            FROM queue.tasks t WHERE t.root_id = '{root}' AND t.module = 'email_logger'"""
    )
    expect(logger == [["done", "0"]], f"the email logger ran and stored no result: {logger}")
    message_id = re.search(rb"^Message-ID:\s*(<[^>]+>)", EMAIL_SAMPLE.read_bytes(), re.I | re.M)
    recorded = sql(
        f"""SELECT count(*) FROM brocess.email_thread_message
            WHERE message_id = '{message_id.group(1).decode()}'"""
    ) if message_id else [["none"]]
    expect(recorded == [["1"]], f"the email logger recorded the email's thread once: {recorded}")
    # and the thread module, which runs for correlation, waited for that record and found the email
    # in it, as ace3's does after its email-mode pass
    thread = sql(
        f"""SELECT o.value, jsonb_array_length(r.details->'messages')
            FROM analysis.results r JOIN analysis.observables o ON o.id = r.observable_id
            WHERE r.root_id = '{root}' AND r.module = 'email_thread_analyzer'"""
    )
    expect(thread == [[message_id.group(1).decode() if message_id else "", "1"]],
           f"the thread module laid out the recorded conversation: {thread}")


def normal_form(root):
    """The root's tree in the normal form, as text."""
    return compose("exec", "-T", "ace", ACE_COMMAND, "root", "normal-form", root, capture=True)


def check_normal_form(text, failures):
    """Checks what the form of a root from this test has to say."""

    def expect(ok, message):
        log(("ok    " if ok else "FAIL  ") + message)
        if not ok:
            failures.append(f"the normal form: {message}")

    form = json.loads(text)
    observables = form["observables"]
    modules = {m for o in observables.values() for m in o["results"]}
    expect(modules >= set(MODULES), f"it has results from all five modules: {sorted(modules)}")
    expect(text == json.dumps(form, indent=2, sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=False) + "\n",
           "its text is what Python's json.dumps writes, so ace3's script can write the same")
    paths = {p: tags for o in observables.values() for p, tags in o.get("paths", {}).items()}
    expect(paths.get("email.rfc822") is not None and any(
        p.endswith("invoice.zip") and "type=email.attachment" in tags for p, tags in paths.items()
    ), f"files keep their paths and yara_meta tags: {sorted(paths)}")
    extracted = [o for o in observables.values()
                 if any(p.endswith("invoice.txt") for p in o.get("paths", {}))]
    expect(len(extracted) == 1 and any(
        r.startswith("extracted_from file:") for r in extracted[0]["relationships"]
    ), "the extracted file says what it was extracted from")
    expect(any(RULE in json.dumps(o["detections"]) or o["detections"]
               for o in observables.values()), "the YARA match's detection is on an observable")
    expect(not re.search(r'"/(tmp|var|opt|home|root|usr|workspace)/', text),
           "it holds no absolute path")
    expect(not re.search(r'"(created_at|completed_at|lease_expires_at|updated_at)"', text),
           "it holds no row timestamp")


class DevTools:
    """A page in the headless browser, over the DevTools protocol: a WebSocket (RFC 6455) client on a
    socket, enough for text frames, which is all the protocol uses."""

    def __init__(self, url, timeout=30):
        match = re.match(r"ws://([^/:]+):(\d+)(/.*)", url)
        if not match:
            raise SystemExit(f"e2e: not a DevTools URL: {url}")
        host, port, path = match.group(1), int(match.group(2)), match.group(3)
        self.sock = socket.create_connection((host, port), timeout=timeout)
        key = base64.b64encode(os.urandom(16)).decode()
        self.sock.sendall(
            f"GET {path} HTTP/1.1\r\nHost: {host}:{port}\r\nUpgrade: websocket\r\n"
            f"Connection: Upgrade\r\nSec-WebSocket-Key: {key}\r\nSec-WebSocket-Version: 13\r\n\r\n"
            .encode()
        )
        head = b""
        while b"\r\n\r\n" not in head:
            chunk = self.sock.recv(4096)
            if not chunk:
                raise SystemExit("e2e: the browser closed the DevTools connection")
            head += chunk
        head, self.buffer = head.split(b"\r\n\r\n", 1)
        if not head.startswith(b"HTTP/1.1 101"):
            raise SystemExit(f"e2e: the browser refused the DevTools connection: {head[:200]!r}")
        self.next_id = 0
        self.events = []

    def _read(self, n):
        while len(self.buffer) < n:
            chunk = self.sock.recv(65536)
            if not chunk:
                raise SystemExit("e2e: the browser closed the DevTools connection")
            self.buffer += chunk
        data, self.buffer = self.buffer[:n], self.buffer[n:]
        return data

    def _frame(self):
        """The next message's text, joining continuation frames."""
        message = b""
        while True:
            first, second = self._read(2)
            length = second & 0x7F
            if length == 126:
                length = struct.unpack(">H", self._read(2))[0]
            elif length == 127:
                length = struct.unpack(">Q", self._read(8))[0]
            payload = self._read(length)
            opcode = first & 0x0F
            if opcode == 8:
                raise SystemExit("e2e: the browser closed the DevTools connection")
            if opcode == 9:
                self._send(10, payload)
                continue
            message += payload
            if first & 0x80:
                return message.decode()

    def _send(self, opcode, payload):
        mask = os.urandom(4)
        header = bytes([0x80 | opcode])
        if len(payload) < 126:
            header += bytes([0x80 | len(payload)])
        elif len(payload) < 1 << 16:
            header += bytes([0x80 | 126]) + struct.pack(">H", len(payload))
        else:
            header += bytes([0x80 | 127]) + struct.pack(">Q", len(payload))
        masked = bytes(b ^ mask[i % 4] for i, b in enumerate(payload))
        self.sock.sendall(header + mask + masked)

    def call(self, method, **params):
        """Calls a method and returns its result, keeping the events that come meanwhile."""
        self.next_id += 1
        self._send(1, json.dumps({"id": self.next_id, "method": method, "params": params}).encode())
        while True:
            message = json.loads(self._frame())
            if message.get("id") == self.next_id:
                if "error" in message:
                    raise SystemExit(f"e2e: DevTools {method} failed: {message['error']}")
                return message.get("result", {})
            if "method" in message:
                self.events.append(message)

    def evaluate(self, expression):
        result = self.call("Runtime.evaluate", expression=expression, returnByValue=True)
        if "exceptionDetails" in result:
            raise SystemExit(f"e2e: the page threw on {expression!r}: {result['exceptionDetails']}")
        return result["result"].get("value")

    def wait(self, what, expression, within):
        return wait_for(what, lambda: self.evaluate(expression), within=within, every=0.2)

    def close(self):
        self.sock.close()


def open_page():
    """A new tab in the browser, as a DevTools connection."""
    port = compose("port", "browser", "9222", capture=True).strip().rsplit(":", 1)[1]
    request = urllib.request.Request(f"http://127.0.0.1:{port}/json/new?about:blank", method="PUT")
    target = wait_for(
        "the browser to answer",
        lambda: _try_json(request),
        within=30,
    )
    # the browser names its own address; it's reached at the published port
    url = re.sub(r"^ws://[^/]+", f"ws://127.0.0.1:{port}", target["webSocketDebuggerUrl"])
    page = DevTools(url)
    for domain in ("Page", "Runtime", "Log"):
        page.call(f"{domain}.enable")
    return page


def _try_json(request):
    try:
        with urllib.request.urlopen(request, timeout=10) as response:
            return json.load(response)
    except OSError:
        return None


def web_request(method, path, body=None, headers=None):
    """One request to the GUI's and the JSON API's port, not following a redirect: its status, headers
    and body."""
    connection = http.client.HTTPConnection("127.0.0.1", int(PORT), timeout=30)
    try:
        connection.request(method, path, body=body, headers=headers or {})
        response = connection.getresponse()
        return response.status, dict(response.getheaders()), response.read().decode()
    finally:
        connection.close()


def sign_in():
    """The analyst's session headers for the JSON API, or None when the login fails."""
    origin = f"http://127.0.0.1:{PORT}"
    form = urllib.parse.urlencode({"username": ANALYST, "password": ANALYST_PASSWORD})
    status, headers, _ = web_request("POST", "/login", form, {
        "Content-Type": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded", "Origin": origin})
    cookie = (headers.get("Set-Cookie") or headers.get("set-cookie") or "").split(";")[0]
    if status != 303 or not cookie:
        return None
    return {"Cookie": cookie, "Origin": origin, "Content-Type": "application/json"}


def started_at(service):
    """When the service's container last started, by Docker's clock."""
    container = compose("ps", "-q", service, capture=True).strip()
    return subprocess.run(
        ["docker", "inspect", "-f", "{{.State.StartedAt}}", container],
        check=True, capture_output=True, text=True,
    ).stdout.strip()


def check_whitelist(email, failures):
    """PLAN.md 5.14's Done check: an entry added through the JSON API applies to the next task with
    nothing restarted, and its audit row names the actor. The entry is the e2e email's sender on the
    email module's sender whitelist, ace3's smtp_from: the email is whitelisted, its analysis stops and
    it doesn't alert. The entry is deleted again, also through the API, before anything else runs."""

    def expect(ok, message):
        log(("ok    " if ok else "FAIL  ") + message)
        if not ok:
            failures.append(f"whitelist: {message}")

    session = sign_in()
    if session is None:
        expect(False, "the analyst signed in")
        return
    started = {service: started_at(service) for service in ("ace", "parsers")}
    entries = "/api/lists/v1/lists/email_sender_whitelist/entries"
    status, _, body = web_request("POST", entries, json.dumps({
        "match": "substring", "value": "ALICE@example.com", "note": "the e2e test's sender",
    }), session)
    if status != 201:
        expect(False, f"adding the entry answered {status}: {body}")
        return
    entry = json.loads(body)["id"]
    try:
        root = submit(email)
        log(f"submitted root {root} with its sender whitelisted")
        seconds = wait_for(f"root {root} to complete", lambda: completed_after(root), within=120)
        log(f"root {root} completed {seconds:.2f}s after it was created")
        for row in tasks(root):
            log("  task " + " | ".join(row))
        tags, directives = sql(
            f"""SELECT array_to_string(tags, ','), array_to_string(directives, ',')
                FROM analysis.observables WHERE root_id = '{root}' AND type = 'file'"""
        )[0]
        expect("whitelisted" in tags.split(",") and "whitelisted" in directives.split(","),
               f"the email module whitelisted the email: tags {tags!r}, directives {directives!r}")
        files, alerted, cancelled = sql(
            f"""SELECT (SELECT count(*) FROM analysis.observables
                        WHERE root_id = r.id AND type = 'file'),
                       alerted_at IS NOT NULL, cancelled_at IS NOT NULL
                FROM analysis.roots r WHERE id = '{root}'"""
        )[0]
        expect(files == "1", f"nothing was extracted from it: {files} file(s) in the root")
        expect(alerted == "f" and cancelled == "t",
               f"its analysis stopped and it didn't alert: alerted {alerted}, cancelled {cancelled}")
        summary = sql(
            f"""SELECT coalesce(summary, '') FROM analysis.results
                WHERE root_id = '{root}' AND module = 'email_analyzer'"""
        )
        expect(summary == [["Email Analysis: (whitelisted email)"]],
               f"its result is ace3's for a whitelisted email: {summary}")
        audit = sql(
            f"""SELECT actor->>'kind', actor->>'name', action FROM service.audit
                WHERE target_kind = 'list_entry' AND target_id = '{entry}' ORDER BY id"""
        )
        expect(audit == [["user", ANALYST, "add_list_entry"]],
               f"the entry's audit row names the analyst: {audit}")
        now = {service: started_at(service) for service in ("ace", "parsers")}
        expect(now == started, f"nothing restarted: {started} then {now}")
    finally:
        status, _, body = web_request(
            "DELETE", f"/api/lists/v1/lists/email_sender_whitelist/entries/{entry}", None, session)
        expect(status == 204, f"the entry was deleted through the API ({status} {body})")
        audit = sql(
            f"""SELECT actor->>'name', action FROM service.audit
                WHERE target_kind = 'list_entry' AND target_id = '{entry}' ORDER BY id"""
        )
        expect(audit[-1:] == [[ANALYST, "delete_list_entry"]],
               f"the delete's audit row names the analyst: {audit}")
        left = sql("SELECT count(*) FROM lists.entries")[0][0]
        expect(left == "0", f"the lists are empty again, as ace3's trees were made: {left}")


def check_gui_command(failures):
    """PLAN.md 5.12: a command started with the analyst's session runs on the parser pool, contained,
    on ace's own command line: --help completes with the usage, and a command that needs what a contained
    process can't have is refused."""
    session = sign_in()
    if session is None:
        log("FAIL  the analyst couldn't sign in for a GUI command")
        failures.append("no session for a GUI command")
        return
    ended = {}
    for line in ("--help", "serve"):
        status, _, body = web_request("POST", "/api/cli/v1/commands",
                               json.dumps({"command": line, "timeout_seconds": 60}), session)
        if status != 202:
            log(f"FAIL  starting `ace {line}` answered {status}: {body}")
            failures.append(f"`ace {line}` didn't start")
            return
        run = json.loads(body)["id"]

        def done(run=run):
            status, _, body = web_request("GET", f"/api/cli/v1/commands/{run}", None, session)
            command = json.loads(body) if status == 200 else {}
            return command if command.get("state") not in (None, "queued", "running") else None

        ended[line] = wait_for(f"GUI command `ace {line}` to end", done, within=90)
    help_run, serve_run = ended["--help"], ended["serve"]
    ok = (help_run["state"] == "completed" and help_run["exit_code"] == 0
          and "Usage: ace" in help_run["output"] and "serve" in help_run["output"])
    log(("ok    " if ok else "FAIL  ")
        + f"`ace --help` ran contained on the parser pool: {help_run['state']}, exit "
        + f"{help_run['exit_code']}, {len(help_run['output'])} characters of output")
    if not ok:
        log(json.dumps(help_run, indent=2))
        failures.append("`ace --help` didn't complete from the GUI")
    ok = (serve_run["state"] == "completed" and serve_run["exit_code"] == 2
          and "doesn't run from the GUI" in serve_run["output"])
    log(("ok    " if ok else "FAIL  ") + "`ace serve` was refused as a GUI command: "
        + serve_run["output"].strip())
    if not ok:
        failures.append("`ace serve` wasn't refused as a GUI command")


def make_analyst():
    """The first user, holding every permission, as an operator makes one (PLAN.md 5.4)."""
    result = subprocess.run(
        [*COMPOSE, "exec", "-T", "ace", ACE_COMMAND, "user", "create-first", ANALYST,
         "--password-stdin"],
        env=ENV, cwd=COMPOSE_FILE.parent, input=ANALYST_PASSWORD + "\n", text=True,
        capture_output=True,
    )
    if result.returncode != 0:
        raise SystemExit(f"e2e: `ace user create-first` failed:\n{result.stderr}")


def has_browser():
    """Whether the Compose file has the browser service. ace4's does; a site's may not yet, and then the
    browser test is skipped, saying so."""
    services = compose("config", "--services", capture=True).split()
    return "browser" in services


def check_live_alert(email, failures):
    """PLAN.md 5.8: a result that lands appears on an open alert page without a reload."""

    def expect(ok, message):
        log(("ok    " if ok else "FAIL  ") + message)
        if not ok:
            failures.append(f"the browser test: {message}")
        return ok

    page = open_page()
    try:
        page.call("Page.navigate", url=f"{GUI_IN_STACK}/login")
        page.wait("the login page", "document.readyState === 'complete' && "
                  "document.querySelector('form[action=\"/login\"]') !== null", within=30)
        page.evaluate(
            "(() => { const f = document.querySelector('form[action=\"/login\"]');"
            f" f.username.value = {json.dumps(ANALYST)}; f.password.value = {json.dumps(ANALYST_PASSWORD)};"
            " f.submit(); })()"
        )
        page.wait("the login", "location.pathname === '/' && document.readyState === 'complete' && "
                  f"document.getElementById('username')?.textContent === {json.dumps(ANALYST)}",
                  within=30)
        log("ok    the browser logged in to the GUI")

        compose("restart", "responder")
        compose("up", "-d", "--wait", "responder")
        compose("pause", "lookups")
        try:
            root = submit(email)
            log(f"submitted root {root} with the network pool frozen")
            try:
                wait_for(
                    f"root {root} to be an alert with its YARA result",
                    lambda: sql(
                        f"""SELECT 1 FROM analysis.roots r WHERE r.id = '{root}'
                            AND r.alerted_at IS NOT NULL AND EXISTS (
                              SELECT FROM analysis.results x WHERE x.root_id = r.id
                              AND x.module = 'yara_scanner_v3_4')"""
                    ),
                    within=120,
                )
            except SystemExit:
                for row in tasks(root):
                    log("  task " + " | ".join(row))
                raise
            page.events.clear()
            page.call("Page.navigate", url=f"{GUI_IN_STACK}/alerts/{root}")
            page.wait("the alert page", "document.readyState === 'complete' && "
                      "document.getElementById('alert-tree') !== null", within=30)
            page.evaluate("window.ace4E2eMarker = 'the page as it was loaded'")
            navigations = len([e for e in page.events if e["method"] == "Page.frameNavigated"])
            before = page.evaluate(
                "[...document.querySelectorAll('#alert-tree .result')].map(r => r.dataset.module)"
            )
            expect("yara_scanner_v3_4" in before and "rdap_analyzer" not in before,
                   f"the open page has the parser pool's results and no RDAP result: {before}")
        finally:
            compose("unpause", "lookups")
        log("let the network pool go; waiting for the RDAP result on the open page")
        try:
            page.wait(
                "the RDAP result to appear on the open page",
                "document.querySelector('#alert-tree [data-module=\"rdap_analyzer\"]') !== null",
                within=120,
            )
            appeared = True
        except SystemExit as error:
            log(str(error))
            appeared = False
        expect(appeared, "the RDAP result appeared on the open page")
        same = page.evaluate("window.ace4E2eMarker") == "the page as it was loaded"
        later = len([e for e in page.events if e["method"] == "Page.frameNavigated"])
        expect(same and later == navigations, "the page wasn't reloaded or navigated")
        refused = [
            e["params"]["entry"]["text"] for e in page.events
            if e["method"] == "Log.entryAdded"
            and re.search(r"Content.Security.Policy|Refused to", e["params"]["entry"]["text"])
        ]
        expect(not refused, f"the page's policy refused nothing: {refused}")
        check_result_pages(page, expect)
        wait_for(f"root {root} to complete", lambda: completed_after(root), within=300)
        check_graph(page, root, expect)
        check_alert_list(page, root, expect)
    finally:
        page.close()


def check_result_pages(page, expect):
    """PLAN.md 5.9: a result's summary in the open alert's tree links to its page, which draws it with
    its module's analysis view, and the page's policy refuses nothing there either."""
    # read every link off the alert's page first, since each one leaves it
    modules = ("yara_scanner_v3_4", "rdap_analyzer")
    hrefs = {
        module: page.evaluate(
            f"document.querySelector('#alert-tree [data-module=\"{module}\"] a.summary')"
            "?.getAttribute('href') ?? null"
        )
        for module in modules
    }
    for module, href in hrefs.items():
        if not expect(bool(href), f"the {module} result links to its page: {href}"):
            continue
        page.events.clear()
        page.call("Page.navigate", url=f"{GUI_IN_STACK}{href}")
        page.wait(f"the {module} result's page", "document.readyState === 'complete' && "
                  "document.querySelector('.analysis-view') !== null", within=30)
        own = page.evaluate(
            "!document.querySelector('.result-page').textContent.includes('has no view') && "
            "document.querySelector('.analysis-view table, .analysis-view .panel') !== null"
        )
        expect(own, f"the {module} result's page draws it with its own view")
        refused = [
            e["params"]["entry"]["text"] for e in page.events
            if e["method"] == "Log.entryAdded"
            and re.search(r"Content.Security.Policy|Refused to", e["params"]["entry"]["text"])
        ]
        expect(not refused, f"the {module} result's page: the policy refused nothing: {refused}")


def check_graph(page, root, expect):
    """PLAN.md 5.13: the alert page's Graph link opens its relationship graph, which vis.js draws from the
    JSON API's graph of the alert. The library holds a node for the alert and for each observable, result
    and tag the alert has, each laid out, the email, its attachment, the domain and each module's result
    among them, and the page's policy refuses nothing and nothing throws."""
    page.events.clear()
    page.call("Page.navigate", url=f"{GUI_IN_STACK}/alerts/{root}")
    page.wait("the alert page", "document.readyState === 'complete' && "
              "document.getElementById('alert-tree') !== null", within=30)
    href = page.evaluate(
        "[...document.querySelectorAll('a')].find(a => a.textContent === 'Graph')?.getAttribute('href')"
        " ?? null"
    )
    if not expect(href == f"/alerts/{root}/graph", f"the alert page links to its graph: {href}"):
        return
    page.call("Page.navigate", url=f"{GUI_IN_STACK}{href}")
    try:
        page.wait("vis.js to draw the graph", "document.getElementById('graph')?.dataset.drawn === 'true'",
                  within=60)
        drawn = True
    except SystemExit as error:
        log(str(error))
        drawn = False
    status = page.evaluate("document.getElementById('graph-status')?.textContent ?? null")
    if not expect(drawn, f"vis.js drew the alert's graph: {status}"):
        return
    state = page.evaluate(
        """(() => {
            const graph = document.getElementById('graph');
            const { network, nodes, edges } = graph.aceGraph;
            const positions = network.getPositions();
            const canvas = graph.querySelector('canvas');
            return {
                labels: nodes.get().map(n => n.label),
                laidOut: nodes.getIds().every(id => Number.isFinite(positions[id]?.x)
                                                    && Number.isFinite(positions[id]?.y)),
                edges: edges.length,
                canvas: canvas ? [canvas.width, canvas.height] : null,
            };
        })()"""
    )
    counts = sql(
        f"""SELECT (SELECT count(*) FROM analysis.observables WHERE root_id = '{root}'),
                   (SELECT count(*) FROM analysis.results WHERE root_id = '{root}'),
                   (SELECT count(DISTINCT t) FROM (
                      SELECT unnest(tags) AS t FROM analysis.observables WHERE root_id = '{root}'
                      UNION SELECT unnest(tags) FROM analysis.results WHERE root_id = '{root}') tags)"""
    )[0]
    observables, results, tags = (int(n) for n in counts)
    labels = state["labels"]
    expect(len(labels) == 1 + observables + results + tags,
           f"the graph has a node for the alert and each of its {observables} observables, {results} "
           f"results and {tags} tags: {len(labels)}")
    wanted = ["file: email.rfc822", "DKIM Signing Domain (email_dkim_signing_domain): example.com",
              *MODULES]
    missing = [label for label in wanted if label not in labels]
    if not any(label.startswith("file: ") and label.endswith("invoice.zip") for label in labels):
        missing.append("file: ...invoice.zip")
    expect(not missing, f"the graph has the email, its attachment, the domain and each module's result: "
                        f"missing {missing} of {sorted(labels)}")
    expect(state["laidOut"] and state["edges"] >= len(labels) - 1 and state["canvas"]
           and min(state["canvas"]) > 0,
           f"vis.js laid out every node on its canvas: {state['edges']} edges, canvas {state['canvas']}")
    refused = [
        e["params"]["entry"]["text"] for e in page.events
        if e["method"] == "Log.entryAdded"
        and re.search(r"Content.Security.Policy|Refused to", e["params"]["entry"]["text"])
    ]
    expect(not refused, f"the graph's policy refused nothing: {refused}")
    thrown = [e["params"]["exceptionDetails"].get("text") for e in page.events
              if e["method"] == "Runtime.exceptionThrown"]
    expect(not thrown, f"nothing on the graph's page threw: {thrown}")


def disposition_elsewhere(root, disposition):
    """Sets an alert's disposition through the JSON API with a key of its own, as another analyst's
    client would, and not through the open page."""
    out = compose(
        "exec", "-T", "ace", ACE_COMMAND, "user", "create-key", "e2e-dispositioner",
        "--grant", "alert:write", capture=True,
    )
    token = next(
        (line.split(": ", 1)[1] for line in out.splitlines()
         if line.startswith("token (shown once): ")),
        None,
    )
    if not token:
        raise SystemExit(f"e2e: `ace user create-key` printed no token:\n{out}")
    request = urllib.request.Request(
        f"http://127.0.0.1:{PORT}/api/alerts/v1/alerts/{root}/disposition",
        data=json.dumps({"disposition": disposition}).encode(),
        method="PUT",
        headers={"Authorization": f"Bearer {token}", "Content-Type": "application/json"},
    )
    with urllib.request.urlopen(request, timeout=30) as response:
        if response.status != 200:
            raise SystemExit(f"e2e: the disposition answered {response.status}")


def check_alert_list(page, root, expect):
    """PLAN.md 5.10: the alert list at / filters the alerts, and its refresh drops an alert that another
    client dispositioned from an open list of open alerts, with no reload, and nothing the page's policy
    refused."""
    row = json.dumps(f"alert-row-{root}")
    rows = "document.querySelectorAll('#alert-list tr[id^=\"alert-row-\"]').length"

    def show(query):
        page.call("Page.navigate", url=f"{GUI_IN_STACK}/{query}")
        page.wait(f"the alert list at /{query}", "document.readyState === 'complete' && "
                  "document.getElementById('alert-list') !== null", within=30)

    page.events.clear()
    show("?f=disposition:OPEN")
    expect(page.evaluate(f"document.getElementById({row}) !== null"),
           "the alert list of open alerts shows the open alert")
    show("?f=description:no-such-alert-in-e2e")
    expect(page.evaluate(rows) == 0, "a filter that matches nothing lists nothing")
    show("?f=disposition:OPEN")
    page.evaluate("window.ace4E2eMarker = 'the list as it was loaded'")
    navigations = len([e for e in page.events if e["method"] == "Page.frameNavigated"])
    disposition_elsewhere(root, "FALSE_POSITIVE")
    log("dispositioned the alert through the API; waiting for the open list's refresh to drop it")
    try:
        page.wait("the refresh to drop the dispositioned alert",
                  f"document.getElementById({row}) === null", within=75)
        dropped = True
    except SystemExit as error:
        log(str(error))
        dropped = False
    expect(dropped, "the open list's refresh dropped the alert dispositioned elsewhere")
    same = page.evaluate("window.ace4E2eMarker") == "the list as it was loaded"
    later = len([e for e in page.events if e["method"] == "Page.frameNavigated"])
    expect(same and later == navigations, "the list wasn't reloaded or navigated")
    refused = [
        e["params"]["entry"]["text"] for e in page.events
        if e["method"] == "Log.entryAdded"
        and re.search(r"Content.Security.Policy|Refused to", e["params"]["entry"]["text"])
    ]
    expect(not refused, f"the list's policy refused nothing: {refused}")


def check_library_diff(failures):
    """That the library diff (PLAN.md 4.8) has teeth. Its full run over the sample set is a separate
    invocation, tools/library-diff/run --all, since it takes as long as the comparison."""
    started = time.monotonic()
    code = subprocess.run([ROOT / "tools" / "library-diff" / "self-test"]).returncode
    log(("ok    " if code == 0 else "FAIL  ") + "the library diff's self-test "
        f"({time.monotonic() - started:.1f}s)")
    if code != 0:
        failures.append("the library diff's self-test failed; see above")


def check_module_inventory(failures):
    """That docs/modules.md names every analysis module section in ace3's config and no other
    (PLAN.md 7.1), with what serves each read of ACE's data (7.2) and a decision for each program
    a module starts (7.3)."""
    command = [ROOT / "tools" / "ace3" / "modules" / "check"]
    if os.environ.get("CI"):
        command.append("--allow-absent")
    if subprocess.run(command).returncode != 0:
        failures.append("the module inventory (docs/modules.md) doesn't match ace3's config; "
                        "see above")


def check_ports_compared(failures):
    """A port that replaces a Python library must have been compared with something."""
    compared = json.loads((WORK / "compare" / "report.json").read_text())["compared_by_module"]
    for module in LIBRARY_PORTS:
        counts = compared.get(module, {})
        log(f"{module}: {counts}")
        if not counts.get("ace3_results") or not counts.get("ace4_results"):
            failures.append(f"{module} was compared with nothing: {counts}")


def give_ace4_the_trees_world():
    """What make-trees gave ace3's tagging and detection modules (PLAN.md 7.6), given to ace4: the
    observables enabled for detection, through the detection API with a key of their own, the tags
    analysts mapped to observables, with SQL, since ace3 has no API for them either, and the site
    tags, which the overlay holds. Returns why it couldn't, or None."""
    sql("DELETE FROM lists.entries WHERE list = 'observable_detection'; "
        "TRUNCATE analysis.observable_tags")
    # ace3's export names each rule's strings by its detection's id, which make-trees made its place in
    # the file from 1 (PLAN.md 7.16), so ace4's entries take the same ids
    left = sql("SELECT count(*) FROM lists.entries")[0][0]
    if left != "0":
        return f"lists.entries holds {left} entries, so the detections can't take the ids ace3's trees have"
    sql("ALTER TABLE lists.entries ALTER COLUMN id RESTART WITH 1")
    out = compose(
        "exec", "-T", "ace", ACE_COMMAND, "user", "create-key", f"e2e-detections-{uuid.uuid4().hex[:8]}",
        "--grant", "detection:write", capture=True,
    )
    token = next((line.split(": ", 1)[1] for line in out.splitlines()
                  if line.startswith("token (shown once): ")), None)
    if not token:
        return f"`ace user create-key` printed no token:\n{out}"
    detections = json.loads((TREES / "detections.json").read_text())["detections"]
    for expected, detection in enumerate(detections, start=1):
        status, _, body = web_request(
            "POST", "/api/observables/v1/detections",
            json.dumps({"type": detection["type"], "value": detection["value"], "expires_on": None,
                        "detection_context": "tools/ace3/trees/detections.json"}),
            {"Authorization": f"Bearer {token}", "Content-Type": "application/json"},
        )
        if status != 201:
            return f"adding the detection {detection} answered {status}: {body}"
        if json.loads(body)["id"] != expected:
            return f"the detection {detection} got the id {json.loads(body)['id']}, not {expected}"
    # the detections are rules of the ruleset too: the core builds them in, and the parser pool
    # switches to that ruleset, before a sample is scanned
    exported = (
        "SELECT key FROM yara.rulesets WHERE id = (SELECT max(id) FROM yara.rulesets) AND "
        "(SELECT sum((t->>'detections')::int) FROM jsonb_array_elements(detection_export->'types') t) = "
        f"{len(detections)}"
    )
    key = wait_for("the core to build the detections into the ruleset", lambda: sql(exported), within=120)[0][0]

    def loaded():
        # the pool's last switch is to that ruleset: an earlier comparison on this stack loaded it too
        switches = [line for line in compose("logs", "parsers", capture=True).splitlines()
                    if "switched to a new ruleset" in line]
        # the line names the ruleset it switched to, then the one it left
        return bool(switches) and key in switches[-1].split("previous")[0]

    wait_for("the parser pool to load the ruleset with the detections", loaded, within=120)
    for mapping in json.loads((TREES / "observable_tags.json").read_text())["tags"]:
        quoted = [mapping[k].replace("'", "''") for k in ("type", "value", "tag")]
        sql("INSERT INTO analysis.observable_tags (type, value, tag) VALUES ('"
            + "', '".join(quoted) + "')")
    overlay = (SITE / "overlay.yaml").read_text()
    missing = [line for line in (TREES / "site_tags.csv").read_text().splitlines()
               if line and f"        {line}\n" not in overlay]
    if missing:
        return f"tests/e2e/site/overlay.yaml's site_tagger csv doesn't have {missing}"
    return None


def compare_with_ace3(threshold=False):
    """Runs `ace compare` over the sample set in a one-off ace container, with the report under
    <work>/compare. Returns its exit code."""
    report = WORK / "compare"
    report.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    # ace3's trees were made against an empty brocess (tools/ace3/trees/brocess.json), and the
    # email logger has recorded this test's email by now
    sql("TRUNCATE brocess.smtplog, brocess.email_thread_message, brocess.email_thread_domain")
    # and with tools/ace3/trees/nrd.json's newly registered domains, as the core's list
    domains = json.loads((TREES / "nrd.json").read_text())["domains"]
    sql("TRUNCATE nrd.domains; INSERT INTO nrd.domains (domain) VALUES "
        + ", ".join("('" + d.replace("'", "''") + "')" for d in domains)
        + " ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING")
    # and with tools/ace3/trees' detections, tags and site tags (PLAN.md 7.6)
    problem = give_ace4_the_trees_world()
    if problem:
        log(f"FAIL  the tagging and detection modules' world: {problem}")
        return 1
    log("ok    ace4 has the detections, tags and site tags ace3's trees were made with")
    # the recorded Splunk job counts requests from when the responder started
    compose("restart", "responder")
    compose("up", "-d", "--wait", "responder")
    command = [
        "run", "--rm", "--no-deps", "--user", f"{os.getuid()}:{os.getgid()}", "-e", "ACE4_API_KEY",
        "-v", f"{ROOT / 'samples'}:/compare/samples:ro",
        "-v", f"{TREES}:/compare/trees:ro",
        "-v", f"{report}:/compare/report",
        "ace", ACE_COMMAND, "compare", "--samples", "/compare/samples", "--trees", "/compare/trees",
        "--report", "/compare/report",
    ]
    if threshold:
        command.append("--threshold")
        if os.environ.get("CI"):
            command.append("--allow-absent")
    code = compose(*command, check=False, exit_code=True)
    log(f"the comparison's report is in {report}")
    return code


def run(email, kill, failures):
    """Submits the email and waits for its root to complete. With kill, freezes the parser pool
    first, kills it once it holds a lease, and starts it again. Returns the root and seconds to
    completion."""
    # the recorded Splunk job answers "running" twice and then "done", counting requests from
    # when the responder started, so each run starts it again to see the same answers
    compose("restart", "responder")
    compose("up", "-d", "--wait", "responder")
    if kill:
        compose("pause", "parsers")
    # as ace3's email collectors mark the email they collected, so the email logger takes it
    original = {"type": "file", "value": hashlib.sha256(email).hexdigest(),
                "directives": ["original_email"]}
    root = submit(email, observables=[original])
    log(f"submitted root {root}{' with the parser pool frozen' if kill else ''}")
    if kill:
        held = wait_for(
            "the frozen parser pool to be given a task",
            lambda: sql(
                f"""SELECT module, lease_owner FROM queue.tasks WHERE root_id = '{root}'
                    AND state = 'running' AND lease_owner LIKE 'parsers/%'"""
            ),
            within=30,
        )
        log(f"the frozen parser pool holds {held}; killing it with SIGKILL")
        compose("kill", "-s", "SIGKILL", "parsers")
        killed_at = time.monotonic()
        compose("up", "-d", "--wait", "parsers")
        log(f"started the parser pool again {time.monotonic() - killed_at:.1f}s after the kill")
    seconds = wait_for(f"root {root} to complete", lambda: completed_after(root), within=300)
    log(f"root {root} completed {seconds:.2f}s after it was created")
    for row in tasks(root):
        log("  task " + " | ".join(row))
    check_root(root, failures)
    if kill:
        # the task the frozen pool held when it was killed, whichever parser module it was
        held_modules = {module for module, _ in held}
        taken_back = [r for r in tasks(root) if r[0] in held_modules and int(r[4]) >= 2]
        ok = bool(taken_back) and all(r[3] == "done" for r in taken_back)
        log(("ok    " if ok else "FAIL  ")
            + f"the killed pool's task ran again and ended done: {taken_back}")
        if not ok:
            failures.append(f"{root}: the killed pool's task didn't run again")
    return root, seconds


def finish(failures):
    if failures:
        log(f"{len(failures)} check(s) failed:")
        for failure in failures:
            log(f"  {failure}")
        return 1
    log("every check passed")
    return 0


def main(argv):
    keep = "--keep" in argv
    compare_only = "--compare" in argv
    WORK.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    commit = make_signatures()
    log(f"signatures at {WORK / 'signatures'}, commit {commit}")
    browser = has_browser()
    if not browser and "ACE4_E2E_COMPOSE" not in os.environ:
        raise SystemExit("e2e: compose.yaml has no browser service")
    build_scanner_images()
    compose("up", "-d", "--build", "--wait", *SERVICES, *(["browser"] if browser else []))
    failures = []
    try:
        make_key()
        wait_for(
            "the core to build the fixture's ruleset",
            lambda: sql(f"SELECT 1 FROM yara.rulesets WHERE commit = '{commit}'"),
            within=120,
        )
        wait_for(
            "the parser pool to load it",
            lambda: "the first ruleset loaded" in compose("logs", "parsers", capture=True),
            within=60,
        )
        if compare_only:
            if compare_with_ace3() != 0:
                failures.append("ace compare couldn't run every sample; see above")
            return finish(failures)
        check_gui(failures)
        make_analyst()
        check_gui_command(failures)
        email = (ROOT / "samples" / SAMPLE).read_bytes()
        first, undisturbed = run(email, kill=False, failures=failures)
        second, killed = run(email, kill=True, failures=failures)
        log(f"completion: {undisturbed:.2f}s undisturbed, {killed:.2f}s with the parser pool "
            f"killed mid-run (lease {LEASE_SECONDS}s)")
        if killed <= undisturbed:
            failures.append("the run with the kill wasn't slower; did the kill land?")
        form = normal_form(first)
        (WORK / "normal-form.json").write_text(form)
        check_normal_form(form, failures)
        killed_form = normal_form(second)
        (WORK / "normal-form-killed.json").write_text(killed_form)
        if form == killed_form:
            log("ok    both roots have the same normal form, killed pool and all")
        else:
            log("FAIL  the roots' normal forms differ; see normal-form*.json in " + str(WORK))
            failures.append("the same email's two roots have different normal forms")
        check_whitelist(email, failures)
        check_scanners(failures)
        if browser:
            try:
                check_live_alert(email, failures)
            except SystemExit as error:
                log(f"FAIL  the browser test: {error}")
                failures.append(f"the browser test: {error}")
        else:
            log("SKIP  the browser test: the Compose file has no browser service")
        if "ACE4_E2E_SITE" not in os.environ:
            check_library_diff(failures)
            check_module_inventory(failures)
            compare_failed = compare_with_ace3(threshold=True) != 0
            check_ports_compared(failures)
            if compare_failed:
                failures.append("the acceptance threshold (docs/acceptance.md) isn't met; see "
                                "above and target/e2e/compare/report.md")
            else:
                log("ok    the acceptance threshold is met: every difference from ace3 is listed "
                    "in differences.md, and every row matched one")
    finally:
        if failures or keep:
            for service in ("ace", "parsers", "sandbox", "lookups", "scanners", "responder",
                            *(["browser"] if browser else [])):
                print(f"----- {service} logs (last 40 lines)")
                print(compose("logs", "--no-color", "--tail", "40", service, capture=True,
                              check=False))
        if not keep:
            compose("down", "-v", "--remove-orphans", check=False)
    return finish(failures)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
